{
  "an6.64:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.64 ",
  "an6.64:0.2": "6. The Great Chapter ",
  "an6.64:0.3": "The Lion’s Roar ",
  "an6.64:1.1": "“Mendicants, the Realized One possesses six powers of a Realized One. With these he claims the bull’s place, roars his lion’s roar in the assemblies, and turns the divine wheel. ",
  "an6.64:1.2": "What six? ",
  "an6.64:1.3": "Firstly, the Realized One truly understands the possible as possible and the impossible as impossible. ",
  "an6.64:1.4": "Since he truly understands this, this is a power of the Realized One. Relying on this he claims the bull’s place, roars his lion’s roar in the assemblies, and turns the divine wheel. ",
  "an6.64:2.1": "Furthermore, the Realized One truly understands the result of deeds undertaken in the past, future, and present in terms of grounds and causes. ",
  "an6.64:2.2": "Since he truly understands this, this is a power of the Realized One. … ",
  "an6.64:3.1": "Furthermore, the Realized One truly understands corruption, cleansing, and emergence regarding the absorptions, liberations, immersions, and attainments. ",
  "an6.64:3.2": "Since he truly understands this, this is a power of the Realized One. … ",
  "an6.64:4.1": "Furthermore, the Realized One recollects many kinds of past lives. That is: one, two, three, four, five, ten, twenty, thirty, forty, fifty, a hundred, a thousand, a hundred thousand rebirths; many eons of the world contracting, many eons of the world expanding, many eons of the world contracting and ex